  "a6": 1,
  "affine_equation": "y^2 + x*y = x^3 + x^2 + 1",
  "every_coefficient_in_F2": true,
  "reason": "All five Weierstrass coefficients are the literals 0 and 1, which are the elements of the prime field F_2 and lie in F_{2^n} for every n. So E is the base change to F_{2^n} of a curve defined over F_2, and the 2-power Frobenius tau(x,y) = (x^2,y^2) maps E(F_{2^n}) to itself: it is an endomorphism. That is the definition of a Koblitz (anomalous binary) curve.",
  "sage_literal": "EllipticCurve(K,[1,1,0,0,1])  # find_points.sage line 8"
